experiment: aimhold
  instrument        aimhold   trial seed 00000000013586c4   6 creatures
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  the question      can a PERFECT controller HOLD F1 at a target on
                    this plant? No learning -- the error is handed over.
  the hypothesis    aimgain found 107 Hz of backlash with IP on and
                    2.0 with it off, against jitter of sd 70-119. So
                    feedback should work with IP OFF and dead-zone
                    with IP ON: an INTERACTION, not a main effect.
  gain              0.0010 k-units/Hz, DERIVED by aimgain, clamp +-0.25

  arm             |F1-target|      BIAS (reach)     WITHIN sd (precision)
  open  IP on      106.1 +/- 0.9      102.1 +/- 0.8       20.7 +/- 0.3
  CLOSED IP on      66.3 +/- 0.8       66.1 +/- 0.8       13.7 +/- 0.2
  scram  IP on     145.4 +/- 1.0      145.4 +/- 1.0       13.8 +/- 0.2
  open  IP off     108.6 +/- 1.1      106.9 +/- 1.5       22.4 +/- 0.8
  CLOSED IP off     41.9 +/- 0.8       40.1 +/- 1.1       13.4 +/- 0.4
  scram  IP off    162.3 +/- 2.0      162.3 +/- 2.0       13.7 +/- 0.5

  error REMOVED by closing the loop (positive = better aim)
    IP on      +39.8 Hz   scrambled control   -39.3 Hz
    IP off     +66.7 Hz   scrambled control   -53.7 Hz
    INTERACTION (off - on)    +26.9 Hz

  REACH (bias) and PRECISION (within-target sd), closed minus open
    IP on    bias   -36.0   sd    -6.9
    IP off   bias   -66.8   sd    -9.0
    precision vs OPEN       IP on   -6.9   IP off   -9.0   (drive)
    precision vs SCRAMBLED  IP on   +0.1 +/- 0.3   IP off   +0.3 +/- 0.6
    precision INFORMATION-specific?   IP on NO   IP off NO

  REFUSED ON THE PRE-REGISTERED BAR. Closing the loop buys REACH --
  the bias falls, information-specifically, and the IP-off interaction
  is real -- but PRECISION does not beat the scrambled control on
  either arm. Any sustained bias cuts the scatter equally well while
  aiming at the WRONG target, so that gain is DRIVE and not
  information.

  REACH is what v62 already bought and it did not become naming. A
  PERFECT error signal, with no learning to blame, does not improve
  the precision of F1 production -- so no LEARNED controller can. The
  feedback line is refused on this actuator, and the hour-scale
  teaching experiment is not worth building.
